  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Given that $F(x,y)=\u27e8xy,y\u27e9$ and $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y},$ calculate $\u2207\\cdot (f\\,F).$",
  "worked_solution": "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n\u2207\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,\u2207\\cdot F+F\\cdot \u2207f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\u2207\\cdot F$ and $\u2207f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207f & =\u27e8{e}^{y},x{e}^{y}\u27e9, \\\\ \u2207\\cdot F & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(xy)+\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(y)=y+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,\u2207\\cdot F+F\\cdot \u2207f \\\\  & =x{e}^{y}(y+1)+\u27e8xy,y\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8{e}^{y},x{e}^{y}\u27e9 \\\\  & =xy{e}^{y}+x{e}^{y}+xy{e}^{y}+xy{e}^{y} \\\\  & =3xy{e}^{y}+x{e}^{y} \\\\  & =x(3y+1){e}^{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
